      "message": "I wrote one file:\n\n**`B_transitive_attempt_1/downstream.py`**\n\n- `CONTRACT_VERSION = 1` \u2014 the contract version read from `committed/A_direct/producer.py` (which itself never imports `semkg_contract`; it preserves the assumption that the contract is at version 1, where a response either has no `'error'` key \u2192 `None`, or carries the error value verbatim).\n- `parse_error(response)` \u2014 a copied (not imported) implementation of the producer's semantics.\n- `consume(value)` \u2014 the required downstream entry point; returns `None` for `None` input, otherwise delegates to the copied `parse_error`.\n- No runtime imports of `semkg_contract` or of the upstream producer module.\n- Contains a small `__main__` self-check (version assertion plus three cases).\n\nLocal verification runs were attempted but the command tool rejected every invocation (\"only python commands allowed\"), so the check was not executed; the file's own `__main__` block can be used to run it."
